1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 a6 6. h3 e6 7. g4 {"Kurajica's early g4 did not worry Najdorf. He employed the same recipe as Mecking in Round 4 and obtained an even better position - the result was another good win for the veteran." (BCM)} d5 8. exd5 (8. e5 Nfd7 $17 {Najdorf}) 8... Nxd5 9. Nde2 Bb4 10. Bg2 $1 (10. Bd2 Nxc3 11. Nxc3 Bd7 $1 $11 {Informator 4/550}) 10... O-O 11. Bd2 Nb6 $1 $146 (11... Nxc3 $2 {( Nc4 - Najdorf)} 12. Nxc3 Nc6 13. a3 Be7 14. O-O $16 {Kurajica-Mecking, rd 4}) 12. Ne4 Be7 13. O-O Nc6 14. b3 $1 (14. Be3 Nc4 {Najdorf}) (14. Bc3 Na4 {Najdorf}) 14... f5 15. gxf5 (15. N4g3 fxg4 16. hxg4 e5 $1 {Najdorf}) 15... exf5 $11 16. N4c3 {( Be3 Najdorf)} Bc5 $1 17. a4 {( a5, Na4)} a5 18. Bf4 Qe7 (18... Qf6 19. Nd5 {Najdorf}) 19. Qd3 Nb4 20. Qg3 $1 Be6 (20... Nxc2 $2 21. Rac1 Nb4 22. Nb5 $16 {Najdorf}) 21. Rad1 (21. Rac1 Rac8) 21... Nxc2 22. Nb5 (22. Bd6 Bxd6 23. Qxd6 (23. Rxd6 f4 $19) 23... Nc8 24. Qxe7 Nxe7 $19 {Najdorf}) 22... Bd7 $1 23. Nec3 $44 Bc6 24. Rd2 Bxg2 (24... Nb4 25. Re2 Qf7 26. Nc7 Rac8 27. Ne6 $18 {Najdorf}) 25. Qxg2 (25. Kxg2 {is the continuation given in Informator. BCM and The Chess Player both give 25 Qxg2.}) 25... Nb4 26. Nc7 Rac8 27. Re2 Qf7 28. Ne6 Rfe8 29. Nxc5 Rxe2 30. Nxe2 Rxc5 31. Qf3 N6d5 32. Rd1 h6 33. Kh2 Rc2 34. Nd4 $4 $19 (34. Rg1 {( Be5)} Qf6 {Najdorf}) 34... Rc3 35. Be3 f4 36. Ne2 fxe3 {Sources: BCM, February 1972, p53; The Chess Player, 1972/2, p17 (Najdorf notes); Informator 13/494 (notes by Minic-Maric - different move 25 Kxg2);} (36... fxe3 37. Qxf7+ Kxf7 38. Nxc3 Nxc3 39. Rd7+ Ke6 40. Rxg7 e2 41. Rg1 Nd3 {Najdorf}) 0-1

